## What was built
A single-root articulated bicycle (root = `frame`) with 11 parts and all primary mechanisms:

**Structure** — diamond frame from real round tubes (down/seat/top/head tubes, chainstays, seatstays, BB shell, dropouts, seat-cluster lug) in gloss-blue paint; a curved two-blade fork with steerer; a swept handlebar with stem and rubber grips; saddle with rails/clamp/nose.

**Wheels** — front and rear use `WheelGeometry` + `TireGeometry` (rim, 24 spokes, domed hub, through-axle, rubber tyre with circumferential tread); the rear adds a freewheel body and drive cog.

**Drivetrain** — BB spindle, two crank arms, steel chainring; a chain loop around chainring and cog.

**Articulations** (realistic limits)
- `frame_to_fork` — REVOLUTE steering about the tilted head-tube axis (±0.5 rad); handlebar rides on it
- `fork_to_front_wheel`, `frame_to_rear_wheel` — CONTINUOUS spin about the axles
- `frame_to_seatpost` — PRISMATIC height adjustment (0–9 cm) carrying the saddle
- `frame_to_crankset` + `crankset_to_pedal_{left,right}` — CONTINUOUS pedalling and free-spinning pedals
- FIXED mounts for handlebar, saddle, chain

**Lettering** — raised "BICYCLE" molded on the down tube (drive side) and on the saddle flank, plus "26 x 1.75" on the front tyre sidewall.

All nested fits (steerer-in-head-tube, seatpost-in-seat-tube, spindle-in-BB-shell, axle/cassette in dropouts, chain on sprockets) are covered by scoped overlap allowances, each paired with an exact `expect_contact` support proof, and pose tests confirm steering swings the bar and the seatpost lifts the saddle.

